🔧 Section A1 – Power Distribution & Protection

Objective: Safely route all high-current lines (AC & DC) and install protective components before signal wiring.

Components

Alternator/Inverter unit

ANL 50 A main fuse + holder

DC bus bar (covered, copper)

AC breaker bank (2 × 15 A 120 V, 1 × 20 A 240 V)

MOV surge absorbers

Ground/neutral bars

AC receptacles (NEMA 5‑15R × 2, 6‑20R × 1)


Assembly Steps

1. Mount Breaker Bank — left enclosure wall, vertical orientation. Torque terminals to 2.3 N·m.


2. Install ANL Fuse Holder within 150 mm of 12 V source.


3. Attach DC Bus Bar on insulating standoffs; cover with clear Lexan guard.


4. Connect 12 V Source → ANL → Bus using 10 AWG red wire; crimp ring lugs (AMP yellow insulated).


5. Install MOVs: L–N, L–PE, N–PE at AC bus input.


6. Mount Ground & Neutral Bars; scrape paint under bonding points.


7. Wire Breakers → Outlets per color codes (black L1, red L2, white N, green PE).


8. Label each breaker and outlet ("120 V R1", "240 V R").




