🧲 Section A3 – Servo Brake Drive

Objective: Install servo actuator and linkage to the magnetic brake lever.

Components

Metal‑gear servo (25–35 kg·cm torque)

Servo bracket & mount hardware

Lever arm (G10 5 mm)

Linear guide rail carriage for flux‑shunt blade

Return spring and silicone bump stops


Assembly Steps

1. Attach servo to bracket (M4 × 12 mm screws + blue thread‑locker).


2. Mount bracket to chassis plate (4 mm Al) and torque 2 N·m.


3. Install 25T horn & lever arm; set neutral 90°.


4. Connect lever → shunt blade carriage with M3 rod end & clevis pin.


5. Spring return: ensure fail‑safe to brake position on power loss.


6. Route servo wiring (16 AWG twisted) through braided sleeving to servo driver.


7. Test actuation: MCU PWM 0–100 % → 8–12 mm travel.


8. Install Mu‑metal shield if within 100 mm of magnetic core.




