🧠 Section A4 – Sensor Pod & Telemetry

Objective: Deploy sensors for feedback and monitoring.

Components

Hall‑effect RPM sensor + magnet flag

NTC temp sensors (core & bearing)

AC voltage/frequency isolation board

Wiring harness (22 AWG shielded pairs)


Assembly Steps

1. Mount Hall sensor 3–5 mm from flywheel target.


2. Epoxy magnet flag onto flywheel surface (2‑part epoxy spray).


3. Place temp sensors with Kapton tape + thermal compound.


4. Install isolation board on standoffs in sensor bay; connect AC tap leads through fused divider.


5. Run shielded cables to MCU I/O header; ground shields at MCU end only.


6. Verify readings: RPM pulse < 50 mVpp noise; temp sensor error < 1 °C.




---

⚡ Section A5 – Output Panel & Receptacles

Objective: Wire and mount the load‑side outputs with proper safety clearances.

Components

2 × NEMA 5‑15R (120 V)

1 × NEMA 6‑20R (240 V)

Ground bus bar

Labels and faceplate hardware


Assembly Steps

1. Cut faceplate openings; deburr.


2. Mount receptacles flush with panel.


3. Wire 120 V outlets: 14 AWG black (L), white (N), green (PE).


4. Wire 240 V outlet: 12 AWG black (L1), red (L2), green (PE).


5. Install breakers inline with each hot lead.


6. Bond grounds to star ground stud (M6 serrated washer stack).


7. Apply labels with voltage rating & breaker current.


8. Perform continuity and polarity test before energizing.




---

🧪 Final System Checks

Torque Audit: verify all fasteners per spec.

Continuity: ring‑out each harness to schematic netlist.

Insulation Test: 500 V megger AC circuits (disconnect electronics).

Ground Bond: < 0.1 Ω panel‑to‑star ground.

Functional Run: Power ON → Start → Brake Test → E‑Stop → Reset.



